13967	{"artifactId":"LLD-ddc4ede1dbf84626-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-ddc4ede1dbf84626-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:19:40.858Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The stakeholder request (open is slow on long history; even the active session should page history out) is fully designed: windowed restore, on-demand older pages, and trimming of the active session, with storage left alone.","evidence":"Today the whole transcript is posted at three sites (chat-panel.ts:423, :913, :932: `post({ type: 'session-restored', sessionId: ..., transcript: session.transcript, mode: permissionMode })`) and the webview replays every row (chat-panel.ts:688). The design replaces exactly that with latestWindow + load-older/transcript-page + trimIfNeeded, and rejects paged storage (a2) as not asked for. No non-goal is built.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The acceptance criteria ac1..ac4 the design maps tests to say what the design assumes they say.","evidence":"The design is standalone; .insrc/artifacts/LLD-ddc4ede1dbf84626-s1.json contains `ac1`..`ac4` only as criterionId entries in acceptanceMapping (5 matches for ac1|ac2|ac3|ac4|acceptance, all in the mapping), and docs/standalone/page-dev-chat-transcript-show-latest-E20261012ddc4ede1/S001 holds only LLD.md and the sequence diagram. No document states the criteria's text, so I could only judge coverage against the quoted user request [[c10]].","action":"State the text of ac1..ac4 in the LLD (or cite the SPEC/triage record that defines them) so the mapping can be checked.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Both event sinks post first and call appendEvent second; in the followed-turn sink appendEvent is outside the `!disposed && session === s` guard; appendEvent returns void.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:394-401: the guard block posts (`else post({ type: 'turn-event', event: ev });`) and `appendEvent(s, ev);` follows outside it. chat-panel.ts:809-811 (runTurn sink): `else post({ type: 'turn-event', event: ev }); appendEvent(s, ev);`. chat-panel.ts:838: `function appendEvent(s: ChatSession, ev: TurnEvent): void`. These are the only two callers.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"recordPermissionOutcome and recordSelectionOutcome post before pushing and post even with no session; runTurn pushes the user row before posting it with key r<index>.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:220-224: `post({ type: 'turn-event', event: { kind: 'permission-outcome', ...} }); if (session !== undefined) { session.transcript.push(...)`. chat-panel.ts:368-372 is the same for selection-outcome. chat-panel.ts:770-779: `s.transcript.push({ role: 'user', ...})` then `post({ type: 'user-row', text: prompt, key: `r${s.transcript.length - 1}` })` under `suppressEcho !== true`.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"line() forces the view to the bottom on every append, and exactly two other sites append to the terminal and force the scroll (renderDiff and the approval-card branch).","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:600 `function line(s,cls){...t.appendChild(d);t.scrollTop=t.scrollHeight;return d;}`; chat-panel.ts:660 renderDiff ends `t.appendChild(box);t.scrollTop=t.scrollHeight;`; chat-panel.ts:672 `if(_c){t.appendChild(_c);t.scrollTop=t.scrollHeight;}`. A search for `t\\.appendChild` and `scrollTop` in chat-panel.ts finds no other site, and no other file under vscode-plugin/src writes scrollTop. The registry appends rows only through the `line` it is handed (render-registry.ts:310, :380, :404, :414, :443, :484, :500, :532).","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A tool-result with no pending tool row renders standalone with its stored command, and a user row or done/error marker clears the pending-tool list, so an older page must render with an isolated pending list.","evidence":"render-registry.ts:443-446: an unpaired result draws `wrap=line('')` with `insrc-toolresult__cmd` when `cmd!==''`. render-registry.ts:389 `register('user',function(vm,host){PEND=[];...` and :379 `if(cc===done||cc===error)PEND=[];`. Without withIsolatedPending, rendering an older page (which starts at a user row) would wipe the live turn's pending tool rows, so the companion the design adds is necessary and correctly motivated.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The paging messages, the index fields and the registry companions are new: nothing equivalent exists today.","evidence":"protocol.ts:66-152 and :155-192 hold no `load-older`, `transcript-page`, `firstIndex`, `total` (on session-restored) or `rowIndex`; `user-row` is `{ type, text, key }` (protocol.ts:151). The registry's returned object (render-registry.ts:544) exposes register, renderRow, collapsible, toViewModel, appendKeyed, resetKeys, onApprovalDecision, approvalPosition, onSelectionDecision: no forgetKeysBefore or withIsolatedPending. Note for the build: HOST_TO_WEBVIEW_TYPES (protocol.ts:195-204) already omits 'approval-position', and protocol.test.ts imports only WEBVIEW_TO_HOST_TYPES, so the HOST_TO_WEBVIEW_TYPES case is a new kind of test there.","action":"None required. Optionally add 'approval-position' to HOST_TO_WEBVIEW_TYPES while touching the list, or say it is left out on purpose.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"__tests__/fake-dom.ts can carry the pager tests driving the real registry, needing only scroll metrics added.","evidence":"fake-dom.ts provides parentNode, firstChild, nextSibling, appendChild, insertBefore (moves an already-parented node, asserts the reference is a child), removeChild, addEventListener plus `fire()` for scroll and click (fake-dom.ts:61-68, :89-91, :138-154); it has no scrollTop, scrollHeight or clientHeight. Two cautions: (1) the registry has never run on this fixture: render-registry.test.ts:24-58 uses its own FakeNode/fakeDocument, so the pager suite will be the first to wrap bodyStub in a `document.createElement`; (2) 'scrollTop grows by exactly the height added' needs scrollHeight to be DERIVED from the children (read-only in the real DOM), which the design does not state.","action":"In the fixture entry, say how the fake computes scrollHeight (for example a fixed height per child) so the prepend test observes the height added instead of setting it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The five row writers and the two appendEvent callers are the complete inventory of places that write a transcript row.","evidence":"A search of vscode-plugin/src (tests excluded) for transcript push/splice/pop/shift finds only chat-panel.ts:222 (permission-outcome), :370 (selection-outcome), :770 (user), :840/:852/:867 (inside appendEvent) and session-store.ts:252 (`append`, which has no caller outside tests). appendEvent is called only at chat-panel.ts:401 and :811. Live posts that write no row (postInfo at :308-311, onError at :830, onWaiting at :798) fall under the design's 'node appended without one takes the latest index seen' rule.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The shell tests that pin the replay need updating only in migration step 6 (switching the restore sites to the latest window); step 5 (embedding the pager) stands on its own.","evidence":"Step 5 itself changes the three shell strings the suite pins: chat-panel.test.ts:1148 `assert.match(html, /setProvLock\\(\\(\\(m\\.transcript\\|\\|\\[\\]\\)\\.length\\)>0\\);/` (step 5 settles the lock from `total`), chat-panel.test.ts:1170 `/reg\\.resetKeys\\(\\);\\(m\\.transcript\\|\\|\\[\\]\\)\\.forEach/` and the [[c7]] pin `/reg\\.appendKeyed\\(reg\\.toViewModel\\(x\\),'r'\\+i\\)/` (step 5 replays with absolute keys through the pager's reset). Any test pinning line()'s `t.scrollTop=t.scrollHeight` breaks there too. So step 5 leaves the suite red until step 6, and is not rollbackable on its own as stated. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"Move the shell-pin updates (chat-panel.test.ts:757 block, :1148, :1170) into step 5 and keep in step 6 only the tests that assert the whole transcript is posted; name these three pins in the session-restored call-site list.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Transcript rows are only ever appended and a session is one whole record under one key, so an absolute index is stable and older stored sessions need no conversion.","evidence":"The only mutations of a transcript are pushes (chat-panel.ts:222, :370, :770, :840, :852, :867; session-store.ts:252); nothing splices, truncates or reassigns it. session-store.ts:195 `void memento.update(SESSION_PREFIX + session.id, session);` writes the whole record; the cap at :202-217 evicts whole sessions, never rows. isSession (session-store.ts:141-151) only requires `Array.isArray(s['transcript'])`, so pre-change records load unchanged.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A row that throws while rendering already falls back inside the registry, and malformed inbound messages are already dropped by type checks, so the load-older validation follows an existing pattern.","evidence":"render-registry.ts:344-347: `try{return r.render(vm,host);}catch(e){try{return REG.fallback.render(vm,host);}catch(_){return null;}}`. handleMessage drops malformed payloads by typeof checks before use: chat-panel.ts:897 `if (typeof msg.provider !== 'string') return;`, :918 `if (typeof msg.chatId !== 'string') return;`, :940, :949. Note renderRow can return null (both renderers threw), so prepend must tolerate a row that produced no node.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"trimIfNeeded's handling is stated for every case, including an active turn with no user row in reach, and the registry state it must forget is complete (only the r<n> keys).","evidence":"The page rule states its fallback ('with none there, keep the plain cut'); the trim rule says only 'removes the oldest nodes back to a user row leaving about 200' and no edge case covers a single active turn past 300 rows (every assistant-delta, tool-call, tool-result and marker writes a row: chat-panel.ts:840-867). Either the trim never fires there (the active session is not paged out) or it cuts plainly, and then the pending-tool list can still hold a removed node: render-registry.ts:409 `PEND.push({wrap:wrap,box:box,...});if(PEND.length>32)PEND.shift();` is cleared only by a user row or a done/error marker (:379, :389), and a later live result attaches inside that detached node and appends nothing: :437-442 `if(pend){...pend.box.appendChild(...);return pend.wrap;}`. The result would be invisible until the page is reloaded. forgetKeysBefore drops only KEYS. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/render-registry.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"State the trim's cut when no user row is in the removable range (plain cut, as for pages), and have the trim also drop pending-tool entries whose node it removes (so a later result renders standalone); add an edge-case row and a pager test for 'one turn longer than 300 rows'.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of ac1..ac4 maps to at least one named test, and the test conventions and fixtures the strategy relies on exist.","evidence":"The acceptance mapping names proving tests for all four ids. The conventions are real: protocol.test.ts:14-18 and :49-53 pin an added kind 'alongside every prior kind' (the pattern cited for load-older); chat-panel.test.ts filters `fc.posted` by payload type for session-restored (:623, :749, :2150) over a fake channel; session-store.ts:260 exports createInMemoryChatSessionStore. The trim gap above (a single turn past 300 rows) has no test, which is covered by that finding's action.","action":"None beyond the test named under error-paths.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":2,"low":12,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-12T07:19:40.858Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
